At the end of an XMLHttpRequest’s body, Ladybird fires a progress event
only if bytes arrived since the last one, or if the body is empty.
Chrome 157 and WebKit (Playwright’s 26.5 build) never repeat an event
either, verified at runtime; each flushes only a still-pending event in
its XMLHttpRequestProgressEventThrottle. Firefox 151 does repeat the
last event when the whole body arrives in one chunk.
